BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Mission Bernal Tasting: Ten Countries in Four Blocks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T200000
DTSTAMP:20261025T205626Z
UID:funcheap-1643337@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Eating Drinking
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerGood Prospect Community ArtFor
  one night\, four blocks of Mission Street become a walking feast. A Missi
 on Bernal Tasting takes you from Cortland Avenue to 29th Street with a tas
 te waiting at every stop: Nepali\, Persian\, Nicaraguan\, Mexican\, Chines
 e\, Japanese\, Greek\, Indian and Italian\, plus local pizza\, beer\, cide
 r and Thai tea. Ten countries in four blocks\, and more than twenty restau
 rants and bars taking part.\nOne ticket covers the whole route. You walk a
 t your own pace\, in any order\, from 5 to 8 pm. Check in any time from 5 
 pm at The Front Porch\, 65 29th Street\, and pick up a map.\n\nThis is a n
 eighborhood fundraiser\, not a promoter’s event. Every dollar goes to a 
 permanent mosaic by Colette Crutcher\, the artist behind the 16th Avenue T
 iled Steps\, on the long-tagged retaining walls at Cortland and Prospect. 
 More than 120 neighbors made tiles for it by hand at free workshops\, and 
 a row of tiles along the base of the mural portrays the small businesses o
 f both corridors.\nThe two previous Taste of Bernal events on Cortland Ave
 nue sold out at 300 tickets. This is the first one on Mission Street.\nTic
 kets: $65 general admission\, $40 for young people and seasoned adults. We
 ar comfortable shoes and come hungry.\n\n$65.00\n\nTickets: https://buytic
 kets.at/prospectstairartproject/2430990\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/
 mission-bernal-tasting-ten-countries-blocks/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/taste-
 flyer.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261025T205626Z
LOCATION:Mission Street between Cortland Ave and 29th St (check in at The 
 Front Porch)\, 65 29th Street\, San Francisco
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/mission-bernal-tasting-ten-countries-blocks/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Black Hammer’s Free “Hopped Up” Trivia Night (Every Wednesda
 y)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1638721@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Eating Drinking
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerBlack Hammer’s Free “Hoppe
 d Up” Trivia Night (Every Wednesday)\nBlack Hammer Brewing\nNo pens\, no
  paper.\nJoin us for three rounds of fast-paced gameshow-style pub trivia 
 in our taproom every Wednesday at 7PM. Free admission\, with bonus points 
 for fastest answer and a live scoreboard.\n\nHopped Up Trivia\nEvery Wedne
 sday at 7pm\nBlack Hammer Brewing\, 544 Bryant St\, SF\nFREE admission\nCh
 eck the website to make reservations and confirm the date.\nPrizes awarded
  for 1st\, 2nd and 3rd place finishers. Always cheer for fastest answer!\n
 Maximum team size is 8 people. Good natured trash-talking encouraged but n
 ot required.\nAbout Black Hammer Brewing\nBlack Hammer Brewing Company bre
 ws and serves award-winning gluten-removed beers that are indistinguishabl
 e from conventional gluten-containing brews. Our taproom\, which has been 
 described as “Cheers on LSD”\, features 16 fresh house-brewed beers on
  tap\, craft empanadas from El Sur\, frittatas (gluten free!) and quiches 
 from Nucha\, and warm soft pretzel sticks served with grain mustard from W
 illkommen\, as well many to-go options. We are dog friendly and offer indo
 or and heated outdoor seating with tons of street parking.\nGet to enjoy t
 heir award-winning beers while enjoying the night with friends!\n\nView th
 is post on Instagram\n\nA post shared by Black Hammer Brewing Company (@bl
 ackhammerbrewing)\n\nUpcoming Black Hammer’s Free “Hopped Up” Trivia
  Night (Every Wednesday) Events\nWed 10/7 Black Hammer’s Free “Hopped 
 Up” Trivia...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://bhb.beer/trivia\nDetails: http
 s://sf.funcheap.com/black-hammers-free-hopped-up-trivia-night-every-wednes
 day-143/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/Trivia
 _May23-23.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Black Hammer Brewing\, 544 Bryant St.\, San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/black-hammers-free-hopped-up-trivia-night-ever
 y-wednesday-143/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Astronomy on Tap San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T210000
DTSTAMP:20261020T194441Z
UID:funcheap-1642711@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Eating Drinking
DESCRIPTION:AoT SF\n\nLocal astronomers talking about stars\, planets\, an
 d the universe at your neighborhood bar. No PhD required.\n\nNOTE: We are 
 at Public Works this month\, with more space for everyone! The event is st
 ill free\, but the venue will ask you to fulfill the 1 drink minimum by bu
 ying a $12 drink ticket.\nAstronomy on Tap is is a free public lecture ser
 ies where astronomers give short\, laid-back talks over drinks at local ba
 rs. No background in science required — our scientists share cool stuff 
 about space while the audience sits back and relaxes\, with plenty of time
  to indulge their curiosity and ask whatever questions they want.\n\nThis 
 month\, we’re hosting:\nNick Rodd (LBL) – The Latest in the Search for
  Dark Matter\nand\nSeth Shostak (SETI Institute) – Are We Alone in the U
 niverse?\nRodd is a Divisional Fellow at Lawrence Berkeley Lab and former 
 faculty member at CERN. Shostak is the senior astronomer for the SETI Inst
 itute\, co-hosts of the weekly podcast Big Picture Science\, and author of
  four books on the search for extraterrestrial life.\nAstronomy on Tap tak
 es place in cities all over the world. This is a revival of the San Franci
 sco chapter\, which regularly hosted events before the pandemic. We’re e
 xcited to be back on a monthly basis!\nThe event is free\, but there is a 
 1 drink minimum. Food (by jeong.sf) will be available with vegetarian opti
 ons.\nIf you’d like to join our mailing list to hear about future events
 \, sign up here.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/astronom
 y-on-tap-sf-october-2026-tickets-2003216296869\nDetails: https://sf.funche
 ap.com/astronomy-tap-san-francisco-3/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/octpin
 k.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261020T194441Z
LOCATION:Public Works\, 161 Erie St.\, San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/astronomy-tap-san-francisco-3/
END:VEVENT
